RF.put("questb:b73",{"8633":{"id":8633,"t":"Enigma Robes","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Husk of the Old God, 2 Idols of the Sun, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Honored reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nHusk of the Old God C'Thun in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of the Sun Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The unmentionable Old God slowly awakens from his slumber beneath Ahn'Qiraj. The terrible fate that awaits Azeroth could come in days or years; time has no meaning for beings of his power.\nWhen the stars are favorable, he will lash out against all living beings with terrible wrath. You must find him before then and find a way to bring his existence to an end.\nDo this and bring me a piece of his husk. I shall grant you armor no mortal has ever worn... armor fit for one who has slain a god!","rew":"You will receive:\nEnigma Robes\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"At his dwelling in Ahn'Qiraj, dread C'Thun awaits in slumber.","done":"I did not expect you to return from your attempt, ‹name›.\nYou've fulfilled a destiny greater than that of most immortal beings.\nBy slaying C'Thun you've not only saved all of Azeroth, you've also tipped the scales of cosmic events beyond your comprehension.\nAccept these robes as a symbol of the glory and burden that will come as a consequence of your actions.\nMay their power aid you in the challenges that await you, god-slayer!\nStart Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Mage Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8633\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Enigma Robes this quest\nBring the Husk of the Old God, 2 Idols of the Sun, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nVethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8793":{"id":8793,"t":"The Horde Needs Your Help!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 10. Gives 650 experience instead of 9,500, 0.07 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Warlord Gorchuk in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits.","desc":"Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Horde needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, ‹name›!\nYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Warlord Gorchuk. What do you say, ‹class›? Will you help out with the vital preparations?","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"Throm'ka, ‹class›! Good to see so many of the Horde, such as yourself, ‹name›, coming out to lend your support in laying the groundwork for the upcoming Ahn'Qiraj War. The effort here will ensure that we are victorious against the Silithid and their evil masters hidden away inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nSo now that you are here, be sure to speak with the various collectors and offer your assistance in gathering those materials that you are suited to.\nUndercity Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":62.6,"y":47.7,"n":"Senior Sergeant Grimsford","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":29.8,"y":67.3,"n":"Warlord Gorchuk","e":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8393":{"id":8393,"t":"Claiming Arathi Basin","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Winning a war is about more than just outsmarting and outfighting your opponent. Victory often comes down to simply producing more than your enemy.\nWhat we have in Arathi Basin is a sizeable supply of resources for whichever side manages to claim it first.\nIf the Alliance comes out victorious, it'll mean more swords and pikes for our troops. If the Horde were to win, those swords and pikes would still get made, they'd just be pointed at us! Now is the time to help the Alliance in Arathi Basin, ‹name›.","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,000\n+100 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Tell me, what are the news from the front?","done":"Good work, soldier! Keep it up and we'll have the Horde running all the way back to Orgrimmar.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"1033":{"id":1033,"t":"Elune's Tear","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Elune's Tear to Pelturas in Astranaar.\nElune's Tear Elune's Tear","desc":"I had hoped Orendil's cure would save Relara, but I fear it only slowed the disease running through my child. We must find more powerful medicine! Thankfully, Orendil spoke to me of further remedies to try should his first one fail.\nElune's Tear is a type of stone that rests in only one place: the isle on Iris Lake, east of Astranaar. Orendil said the stone will wash away corruption... please, ‹name›, bring me Elune's Tear and pray it will end my child's sickness!","rew":"Money: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,750\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"‹name›, did you find Iris Lake? Do you have the Tear?","done":"Oh, you found it! I will place the tear in a stew, and pray that it will cure her.\nThank you! Thank you, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":37.4,"y":51.8,"n":"Pelturas Whitemoon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"713":{"id":713,"t":"Coolant Heads Prevail","lv":37,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Frost Oil and bring it to Lotwil Veriatus in Badlands.\nFrost Oil Deadwood Gardener 0 % , Tar Creeper 0 % , Vilebranch Witch Doctor 0 %","desc":"Let me tell you something about Frost Oil: nothing can keep an engine or gears from overheating quite like it.\nIts cooling properties are extraordinary, and its longevity as a lubricant without equal. That's not all: it also aids in retaining enchantments on magical items.\nI need a vial of it to increase the magical capacity of my shackles and make them powerful enough to stop our summoned friend from killing us all.\nBro'kin, a goblin friend of mine, can teach you to make it. He's in Alterac.","rew":"Experience: 2,850","back":"Have you found the oil I need? It would be so helpful if you were able to find some.","done":"Stupendous! This should be the perfect coolant for my new bracers. If the enchantments don't last a century, then I'll give all my belongings to Servo.\nAll the mages of the Assembly will be in such awe after I finish this, ‹name›. You just wait and see.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":25.9,"y":44.9,"n":"Lotwil Veriatus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"793":{"id":793,"t":"Broken Alliances","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Sign of the Earth to activate the Pillars of Diamond, Opal, and Amethyst and obtain the Runestones.\nPlace the runestones in the Seal of the Earth to free Blacklash and Hematus.\nSlay them and return Blacklash's Bindings, the Chains of Hematus, and the Sign of the Earth to Gorn.\nBlacklash's Bindings Blacklash\nChains of Hematus Hematus\nSign of the Earth Boss Tho'grun\nProvided: Sign of the Earth","desc":"The Seal of the Earth is held by three runestones, held in the Pillars of Diamond, Opal, and Amethyst in Lethlor Ravine. Using the Sign of the Earth, you will be able to remove the runestones and unlock the Seal of the Earth.\nBe wary though, ‹name›, the black drakes Blacklash and Hematus are not to be trifled with. See them dead and return their bindings to me.\nTo reach the ravine, travel to the far eastern part of the Badlands. Be careful though, for the ravine is home to countless drakes.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBlazewind Breastplate Prismscale Hauberk Warforged Chestplate Mindburst Medallion\nExperience: 5,900\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"There are few enemies more deadly than dragonkind, and there were few dragons that fought as ferociously as Blacklash and Hematus.","done":"The black dragonflight continues to ally with the renegade Blackrock orcs, and both must be brought into line, or removed. With Blacklash and Hematus dead, we can turn our attentions westwards, towards Blackrock Spire.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":2.9,"y":45.6,"n":"Gorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"8313":{"id":8313,"t":"Sharing the Knowledge","lv":57,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Torn Recipe Page to Calandrath at the inn in Cenarion Hold.\nTorn Recipe Page\nProvided: Torn Recipe Page","desc":"While the recipe for cooking sandworm meat is legible, it contains references to herbs and spices you've never heard of. Calandrath might have enough knowledge of the plants that grow in the desert to make sense of it.","rew":"You will learn: Smoked Desert Dumplings\nMoney: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,000\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you learn the recipe? You won't keep it to yourself, I hope!","done":"Let's have a look at that...\nThis seems simple enough. They have their own names for some of the herbs, but those are simple enough to figure out. Here, let me show you!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":37.9,"y":45.3,"n":"Sandy Cookbook","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":51.9,"y":39.2,"n":"Calandrath","e":1}],"cats":["cooking"]},"94233":{"id":94233,"t":"Craftsmans writ practice lock","min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Practice Lock\nPractice Lock","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Practice Lock, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"I watched this whole place get burned to the ground and that keep toppled over. It was glorious.\nNever expected a group of bandits to try using this place as a base of operations.","done":"Ahh, my practice lock has arrived.\nThe Syndicate here have been plotting to turn this place into a prison like it once was. I already know that at least one orc is currently being held here. Maybe more. I don't intend to be another, but I intend to be more prepared than the last time if they catch me off guard.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":80,"y":48.7,"n":"Gorgrash","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94313":{"id":94313,"t":"Craftsmans writ white bandit mask","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: White Bandit Mask\nWhite Bandit Mask","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 White Bandit Mask, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: White Bandit Mask Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94313","cats":["crafting"]},"953":{"id":953,"t":"The Fall of Ameth'Aran","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Study the tablets which tell of Ameth'Aran and of its fall, then return to Sentinel Tysha Moonblade in Darkshore.\nRead the Lay of Ameth'Aran\nRead the Fall of Ameth'Aran","desc":"To the east you will find the ruins of Ameth'Aran. It is now inhabited by the restless spirits of the Highborne that once dwelt within its walls, but once it was a place where the servants of Azshara freely practiced their powerful magics.\nI was sent to explore the ruins and came across two large tablets, scrawled with the stories of Ameth'Aran and its fall. While I read the runes, I was accosted by the spirits, and fled.\nPlease, if you can, venture to the ruins and decipher the tablets in my place.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"When you have studied the tablets and learned of Ameth'Aran's fall, I will take the knowledge on to Auberdine, and inform the Circle of Ancients.","done":"We have few records from the time around the War of the Ancients, especially near the destruction of the Well of Eternity. Given the upheaval and cataclysmic events that were taking place, it is no big surprise.\nThank you, ‹name›. With your help, my work here is finished, and I will be able to deliver a full report to the Circle.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":40.3,"y":59.7,"n":"Sentinel Tysha Moonblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"94873":{"id":94873,"t":"Buying friendship gelkis","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Totem Tote to the Gelkis Quartermaster at Gelkis Village in the Desolace to significantly increase your reputation with that clan. You must be of at least Neutral standing with the Gelkis Clan Centaur.\nProvided: Totem Tote","desc":"Either dominant centaur clan is likely to pose a good ally, but I ought to offer a word of caution regarding the Gelkis.\nI have trustworthy intel that suggests, between the Magram and the Gelkis, the latter are very much on the losing side. This may work to our advantage--desperation may push the isolated clan into opening up to outside help.\nI have prepared a tote of totems for you to take to their quartermaster, assuming they have one, in Gelkis Village. This may work in our favor.\nLevel 45 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 41 43 48 57 Side Both factions Quest ID 94873","cats":["desolace"]},"1193":{"id":1193,"t":"A Broken Trap","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Thorium Widget Wildspawn Shadowstalker 0 % , Gordok Warlock 0 % , Thuzadin Shadowcaster 0 % in Stratholme , Blackhand Iron Guard 0 % and 2 more\nFrost Oil Deadwood Gardener 0 % , Tar Creeper 0 % , Vilebranch Witch Doctor 0 %","back":"A large, broken trap lies before you. From the looks of it, the ogres have tried to repair the trap but to no avail. A hastily written note lies next to the trap, and strangely enough it details exactly what is needed to repair it: a thorium widget and some frost oil. Were the trap repaired, an ogre passing near it might get trapped, and could be avoided.\nClearly, it would seem fortuitous that very few ogres know how to read.\nClearly.","done":"The thorium widget slides effortlessly into place, creating a conduit to pour the frost oil down. Once the last drops of oil have been emptied into it, the trap snaps into position.\nWoe be to any unwary ogre that should just so happen to wander by!\nStart Broken Trap End Broken Trap Level 60 , requires level 56 Difficulty 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 1193","cats":["dire-maul"]},"98393":{"id":98393,"t":"The great cat spirit","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.","desc":"It would seem that you are ready for the next step in your journey, young druid. Dendrite Starblaze has sent for you, and wishes for you to seek him out in Moonglade once again.\nYou have already learned to call upon the magic to take you to Moonglade, so you should be able to embark immediately if you choose. I would suggest you leave soon, if you wish to continue your druidic training.","done":"And so it continues, Father Cenarius.\n<Dendrite makes a quick, invisible gesture in the air above him. A slight aura of power falls over him.>\nGreetings again, Hans. It is time for you to learn the next perspective of nature: the cat. I will put you on the path to understanding this aspect of druidic life, but much like the bear, it is you that must embrace this learning and propagate it.\nDarnassus Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.2,"y":8,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.4,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"7673":{"id":7673,"t":"Frost Ram Exchange","lv":1,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Frost Ram","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSwift Brown Ram Swift Gray Ram Swift White Ram","back":"[PH] Ye bring me yer old ram, I will trade it in for one from the new pack! The new ram will be just as fast as yer old one, but with a new look to him. You can look at the swift rams here to see what ye will have to choose from.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":50.6,"n":"Veron Amberstill","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"233":{"id":233,"t":"Coldridge Valley Mail Delivery","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the stack of letters to Talin Keeneye.\nA Stack of Letters\nProvided: A Stack of Letters","desc":"Hm, I don't suppose you'd be willing to do a favor for me, lad/lass? A stack of letters came through the pass today, but I don't have the time to send them along.\nThey're all addressed to Talin Keeneye. You can find him to the west down the road. He's set up camp next to the frozen lake.\nWhat do you say?","rew":"Experience: 190\n+75 reputation with Ironforge\n+75 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Yes? Do you have something for me?","done":"Thank you, I've been waiting for these letters for quite some time...\nUnfortunately, these letters aren't all for me. This one is addressed to Grelin Whitebeard. He's not too far away if you'd like to deliver it to him.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.9,"y":71.2,"n":"Sten Stoutarm","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":22.6,"y":71.4,"n":"Talin Keeneye","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"313":{"id":313,"t":"The Grizzled Den","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 8 Wendigo Manes and bring them to Pilot Stonegear.\n8 Wendigo Mane Edan the Howler 60 % , Vagash 60 % , Old Icebeard 60 % , Wendigo 60 % and 1 more","desc":"Driving a Siege Engine isn't for everyone. It takes an iron grip and nerves of steel...lucky I have both! How about you? How's your mettle? Want to prove it to me?\nWell...I'm looking to make my engine, Trollplow, a little more cozy. How about you get me a heap of Wendigo Manes from the Grizzled Den, west of Kharanos. Those manes would make a great rug for Trollplow's inside deck!","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Hey, ‹name›. Been to the Grizzled Den yet? Those Wendigos can be fierce.","done":"Ah yes, these manes will work great! You show a lot of grit, ‹class› - I wager we'll see great things from you.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":49.6,"y":48.6,"n":"Pilot Stonegear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"96873":{"id":96873,"t":"A pain in the neck","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Pa'zula in Sen'jin Village wants you to collect 3 Luminous Residue. Luminous Residue can be obtained by disenchanting Hexed Pendants dropped by trolls in the Echo Isles.\n3 Luminous Residue","desc":"The trolls east of here have lost their will to the witchdoctor, Zalazane. He uses many cruel magics to keep hold of his prisoners' minds, but one of his favorite tricks is to make them wear pendants wrapped in evil binding spells.\nPractice your enchanting skills by stripping the magic from these pendants, and bring me the results. And don't accidentally put one around your neck, if you value your freedom!","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 525\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"What do you have for me, Thay?","done":"Fine work. A shame about the slain trolls, but with the binding spells removed, their spirits can rest.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":56.6,"y":73.6,"n":"Pa'zula","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"1273":{"id":1273,"t":"Questioning Reethe","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go with Ogron to speak with Reethe, then return to Krog in Brackenwall Village.","desc":"It took a long time, but I found Reethe. He hide good for a human.\nOgron worried that he might be crazy after so much time in swamp. You come with me for we go get answers from him.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEyepoker Blasting Hackbut\nExperience: 3,550","back":"Did you find Reethe?","done":"Hmph. It is good that Reethe will no longer be lurking around the swamp, but it is a shame that humans are built so frail that he could not recover from a little arrow wound.\nIt seems that this thread of the mystery has led nowhere, and we must look elsewhere.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":41,"y":36.7,"n":"Ogron","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.4,"y":31.9,"n":"Krog","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5513":{"id":5513,"t":"Mantles of the Dawn","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Argent Dawn Valor Tokens to Quartermaster Breechlock at Light's Hope Chapel, Eastern Plaguelands.\n10 Argent Dawn Valor Token\nReach 21000 reputation with Argent Dawn","desc":"Your service to the Argent Dawn is to be commended, ‹name›. You are truly revered amongst us. I have been authorized to make available for you to purchase one of the Dawn's most valued items - our magic resistance mantles.\nApplication of a mantle to your existing shoulder piece will enhance your resistance to the powers of magic in one of five potential ways. As a sign of continued dedication to our cause, I ask for no less than ten of our valor tokens in exchange for access to these mantles.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Ah, noble ‹class›! Have you brought the valor tokens requested of you? Once you hand them to me, I will make our various mantles available to you for purchase.","done":"Outstanding - your tribute to the Dawn is duly noted, ‹name›. With this accomplished, I am delighted to make our mantles available to you for purchase. So long as you maintain your current status with us, these mantles will be purchasable from any authorized quartermaster of the Argent Dawn.\nFor the Dawn, my brother/sister!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.8,"y":50.2,"n":"Quartermaster Miranda Breechlock","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"91753":{"id":91753,"t":"An enchanting lesson","lv":7,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kitta Firewind in the Tower of Azora wants you to collect 3 Luminous Residue.\nLuminous Residue can be obtained by disenchanting Crude Wax Effigies dropped by Kobold Geomancers.\n3 Luminous Residue","desc":"Academic rigor is of course essential to the enchanter's craft, but a practical foundation can pay dividends. Consider, as an example, the lowly Kobold. Lacking formal education, they nevertheless demonstrate a sort of innate aptitude for simple cantrips and enchantments.\nObtain some of their wax effigies and deconstruct the enchantments bound within them. You may find it elucidating.","rew":"Money: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 480\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What have your studies revealed?","done":"Theory and practice are two sides of a coin, Spineblast. Remember this.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":64.8,"y":70.6,"n":"Kitta Firewind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"2953":{"id":2953,"t":"More Sparklematic Action","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -1g -3s instead of 0.","obj":"Grime-Encrusted Object Holdout Technician 25 % , Holdout Medic 25 % , Holdout Warrior 25 % , Irradiated Pillager 25 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nSparklematic-Wrapped Box","back":"The Sparklematic 5200 is empty, awaiting a grime-encrusted object to clean and three silver coins to start!","done":"The Sparklematic 5200 comes to life, lurching to and fro. Inside, the helpless grime that has encrusted the object placed within it is being pulverized by the machine's gnomish cleaning agent.\nThe Sparklematic 5200 comes to a halt, heralded by a familiar \"ding!\" The item receptacle of the machine spirals open, revealing a neatly wrapped box.\nStart The Sparklematic 5200 End The Sparklematic 5200 Level 30 , requires level 25 Difficulty 25 26 28 33 38 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 2953\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 30, 2,450 XP in all.\n1 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200!\nInsert a Grime-Encrusted Item into the Sparklematic 5200, and be sure to have three silver coins to start the machine.\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200!\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2,450 XP\n3 [ 30 ] More Sparklematic Action this quest\nThe Sparklematic 5200","cats":["gnomeregan"]},"553":{"id":553,"t":"Helcular's Revenge","lv":33,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Charge the Rod of Helcular with the powers of the Flame of Azel, Flame of Veraz and the Flame of Uzel.\nDrive the charged rod into Helcular's grave in Southshore.\nRod of Helcular\nFlame of Azel charged\nFlame of Veraz charged\nFlame of Uzel charged\nProvided: Rod of Helcular","desc":"Here, take the Rod of Helcular. You will need it.\nHelcular fashioned 3 ceremonial pyres as part of his most powerful spell. The Flame of Azel and the Flame of Veraz lie within the Foothill Caverns. The Flame of Uzel lies in a cave above the caverns, further north in the mountains.\nThe Rod of Helcular must be charged from each of the three flames. Once the ritual is complete, drive the rod into Helcular's grave in Southshore, the heavily guarded human town to the south. Vengeance shall be ours!","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"Helcular's grave teems with a mystical energy.","done":"A great rumbling emanates from the ground.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":63.9,"y":19.7,"n":"Novice Thaivand","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":52.8,"y":53.4,"n":"Helcular's Grave","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6073":{"id":6073,"t":"The Hunter's Path","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Dazalar in Dolanaar.","desc":"Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.\nYou must see Dazalar in Dolanaar. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Yes, it is time, ‹class›.\nDarnassus Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":42.2,"y":7.3,"n":"Dorion","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.7,"y":59.5,"n":"Dazalar","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"94793":{"id":94793,"t":"Training the beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Isaac Chan in Goldshire.","desc":"You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it. For this, there is none better than Isaac Chan, a lifelong woodsman. He will give you the ability to train your new pet.\nGo with the winds, young ‹class›.","done":"A fledgling ‹class›, I see. Yes, I can bestow you with the skills you need to train and guide your pet. Not only will you be able to teach your pet new abilities, you will now be able to feed your pet, as well as revive it, should it fall in battle.\nRemember, Darlin, always respect the balance and live in awe of nature around you. Now, go forth. We shall speak again, at a later date.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.2,"y":66.2,"n":"Josephine Carson","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.8,"y":66.4,"n":"Isaac Chan","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"8153":{"id":8153,"t":"Courser Antlers","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a pair of Perfect Courser Antlers to Ogtinc in Azshara. Ogtinc resides atop the cliffs northeast of the Ruins of Eldarath.\n2 Perfect Courser Antler Mosshoof Courser 8 %","desc":"The courser wears the mightiest antlers in the known lands. Such antlers are used to defend the courser, goring an attacker and often damaging the points. Perfect, natural antlers are the sign of an animal spirit with supreme confidence.\nTo hold such antlers will bestow the same confidence in you.\nHunt the mosshoof courser, find the perfect antlers and bring them to me.","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"Have you found the antlers?","done":"You must possess keen sight and great patience to have obtained these. Well done.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":42.4,"y":42.6,"n":"Ogtinc","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"98313":{"id":98313,"t":"For further study","lv":32,"min":24,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Whelgar Relic Package to Historian Karnik in Ironforge.\nProvided: Whelgar Relic Package","desc":"Whatever this is all about, ‹name›, it's epic stuff alright.\nI'll bundle everything up nice for you. Take it to Historian Karnik in the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge. You'll usually find him in the back, nose-deep in some tome or another in the library.\nIt'll take a downright army to crack the case on this one, but if what we've seen so far is any indication it will well be worth it!\nWetlands Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":38.8,"y":52.2,"n":"Prospector Whelgar","s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":77.2,"y":11.8,"n":"Historian Karnik","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8953":{"id":8953,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Deliana in Ironforge with a set of Magister's Boots, Magister's Leggings and Magister's Mantle.\nMagister's Boots Hearthsinger Forresten 0 % in Stratholme\nMagister's Leggings Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nMagister's Mantle\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the medallion back together. Return to Deliana and tell her that Bodley is her only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to her about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nSorcerer's Boots Sorcerer's Leggings Sorcerer's Mantle\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're back, ‹name›. You must tell me all about what you've found out. But first let us arrange for your reward.","done":"I can't believe our lives are all but forfeit all because of a stupid medallion! And you're sure Anthion mentioned Bodley?\nWell, you've done your job so let's get your reward out of the way.\nEastern Plaguelands Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8713":{"id":8713,"t":"Starsong the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?\nStart Elder Starsong End Elder Starsong Level 60 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 56 58 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 8713","cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8873":{"id":8873,"t":"The Lunar Festival","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to the Lunar Festival Harbinger in the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar. You can also talk to Lunar Festival Harbingers in other capital cities.","desc":"It's that time of the year, ‹name›! The Cenarion Circle invites all denizens of Azeroth to partake in our celebration of the Lunar Festival. You will find the Lunar Festival Harbinger in this very city at a location marked by a blessed circle of moonlight. She can tell you more about the holiday.","done":"Welcome, ‹name›. Are you here to join in the festivities?\nOrgrimmar Thunder Bluff Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":40.8,"y":30.5,"n":"Lunar Festival Herald","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":41.7,"y":32,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":38.4,"y":63.4,"n":"Lunar Festival Herald","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":71.1,"y":28.2,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.8,"n":"Lunar Festival Herald","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.7,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9113":{"id":9113,"t":"Circlet of Faith","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Circlet of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Circlet, 15 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 3 Mooncloth and 3 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Circlet\n15 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n3 Mooncloth\n3 Nexus Crystal","desc":"<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\nBlessed boy/girl, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.","rew":"You will receive:\nCirclet of Faith\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Circlet of Faith.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Father Inigo Montoy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9033":{"id":9033,"t":"Echoes of War","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,500, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants you to slay 5 Living Monstrosities, 5 Stoneskin Gargoyles, 8 Deathknight Captains and 3 Venom Stalkers.\nDeathknight Captain slain : 0/ 8 in Naxxramas\nVenom Stalker slain : 0/ 3 in Naxxramas\nLiving Monstrosity slain : 0/ 5 in Naxxramas\nStoneskin Gargoyle slain : 0/ 5 in Naxxramas","desc":"Five years since the last war...\nTens of thousands of lives were lost and for what? The threat was never fully extinguished.\nAnd so the Lich King stirs once more... His yes-man, Kel'Thuzad, amassing for another attack upon our lands.\nWe will not allow it! Prove your dedication. Prove that you are willing to risk life and limb to stop this madness and the combined might of the Dawn and the Crusade will be at your beck and call.\nEnter Naxxramas and destroy the Scourge within...","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Duty, honor, dedication... What do these words mean to you?","done":"A job well done! You will be rewarded via the services of the men and women at Light's Hope.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"1433":{"id":1433,"t":"Alliance Relations","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Maurin Bonesplitter in Desolace.","desc":"The Burning Blade have many agendas, but know that they are evil to their core, their spirits corrupted, and their destruction is the only way to thwart their objectives.\nKeldran sent Maurin with me because of his knowledge of the Blade and their warlock ways.\nHe has control of our plots against the Blade while I deal with the other demonic threats here in Desolace.\nSpeak to him, and he will guide you in his designs.","rew":"Experience: 270","done":"Ah, yes. Aid from those loyal to the Warchief is always appreciated.\nMy name is Maurin. I am here at the behest of Keldran and the Warchief cub Thrall. It is my desire to aid the youngling leader against the evils that threaten his rule.\nCome, come closer, ‹class›. I shall explain to you my plan for removing the festering boil that is the Burning Blade.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":52.6,"y":54.4,"n":"Takata Steelblade","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":52.2,"y":53.4,"n":"Maurin Bonesplitter","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"7833":{"id":7833,"t":"A Donation of Wool","lv":60,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Wool Cloth Farrin Daris 66.7 % , Adam Lind 62.1 % , Mountaineer Langarr 57.1 % , Protector Leick 47.6 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 650\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"We are currently accepting donations for wool cloth. A donation of sixty pieces of wool cloth will net you full recognition by Darkspear Trolls for your generous actions. Our stores are such on wool that we would only need sixty pieces from you total; we should be able to acquire enough from others in the realm to support our drive.\nIf you have the sixty pieces of wool cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":37.7,"y":87.9,"n":"Vehena","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"5673":{"id":5673,"t":"Elune's Grace","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.","desc":"You know you have access to any of our trainers at any time, ‹name›, but there are some things that we cannot pass on to you. One of those things are the teachings of your goddess Elune. She gives special abilities to her faithful, and if I'm not mistaken, it is time for you to return home to your Temple of the Moon to be tested.\nReturn there when you can and speak to Priestess Alathea.","rew":"You will learn: Elune's Grace\nExperience: 390","done":"Elune bless you for returning so quickly to us. This is an important time in your training, and a time that all of our order take very seriously. When you've rested from your journey here, please, let me know. We can then discuss the continuation of your training and where your path will lead you next.\nStormwind City Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":44.6,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Priestess Alathea","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"3113":{"id":3113,"t":"Encrypted Memorandum","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Encrypted Memorandum and speak to Solm Hargrin in Coldridge Valley.\nEncrypted Memorandum\nProvided: Encrypted Memorandum","desc":"While you were helping me out, this memorandum was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the rogue trainer Solm. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Glad to see you got my note and came over. Sorry about pretendin' it was a memorandum from your higher-ups... no offense intended. I just knew the two of us, along with others of our kind, gotta stick together.\nNot many think it's the best thing in the world to have your kind and my kind holed up in the same city, but I think we can work things out just fine. What do you think?","done":"I pretty much keep to myself around here so we don't get a bad wrap for things gone missing, but if you need anything, some training or somethin', just come back anytime.\nYou and me got an understandin'. We know when it comes down to it you can only trust family... and that's just what we got going on here, isn't it? Regardless of Gnomeregan being... overrun, and whatever else is thrown our way, we got one another to back each other up. Right?","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.9,"y":71.2,"n":"Sten Stoutarm","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.4,"y":67.5,"n":"Solm Hargrin","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"8233":{"id":8233,"t":"A Simple Request","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Lord Jorach Ravenholdt in Ravenholdt Manor.","desc":"Lord Jorach Ravenholdt has requested your presence. The matter is secret, and I cannot say any more.\nRavenholdt Manor is located in the Hillsbrad Foothills -- look for a path in the mountains northwest of Durnhold Keep.","rew":"Experience: 500\n+10 reputation with Ravenholdt","done":"Welcome, welcome, welcome! Please, ‹name›, have a seat and discuss a simple matter with me.\nYou see, ‹name›, I've recently lost something dear to me, and to put it bluntly, I want it back at all costs. There's something in it for you, don't worry about that! Oh yes, something very nice.\nNow, what say you ‹name›... are you up for some adventure?\nOrgrimmar Darnassus Undercity Dun Morogh Stormwind City Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":43.9,"y":54.6,"n":"Ormok","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":37.9,"y":20.9,"n":"Anishar","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":85.2,"y":71.6,"n":"Miles Dexter","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.6,"y":23.5,"n":"Ormyr Flinteye","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.3,"y":68.6,"n":"Lord Tony Romano","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":86,"y":78.9,"n":"Lord Jorach Ravenholdt","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"1113":{"id":1113,"t":"Hearts of Zeal","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity wants 20 Hearts of Zeal.\n20 Heart of Zeal Scarlet Monk 80 % in Scarlet Monastery , Scarlet Torturer 80 % in Scarlet Monastery , Scarlet Abbot 80 % in Scarlet Monastery , Scarlet Champion 80 % in Scarlet Monastery and 4 more","desc":"Why do I need a rare type of guano, you might ask. Well, for this experiment I want to see what effect two diametrically opposed chemical substances can have on each other, especially when both are combined with an ever-toxic agent to ensure the most... ghastly results.\nIn the northeastern peaks of Tirisfal Glades lies the Scarlet Monastery. There the crazed disciples of the Scarlet Crusade congregate, both inside and outside the halls. Which you slay matters not, any of them may have the heart I need.","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you returned from the Scarlet Monastery? I'll need many hearts for this delightful experiment!\nNo doubt, Varimathras and the Dark Lady will be pleased to be rid of the Scarlet Scum as well...","done":"My what an abundance of gore you have brought me, ‹name›! Your efforts have been most excellent!\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":48.8,"y":69.3,"n":"Master Apothecary Faranell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scarlet-monastery"]},"94473":{"id":94473,"t":"Fire sapta","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Braldir Ashmantle for another Fire Sapta","rew":"You will receive:\nFire Sapta","done":"May fire burn within your heart, Ukko.\nThe elements await you.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":32,"y":66,"n":"Braldir Ashmantle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"92873":{"id":92873,"t":"Proof of concept","lv":41,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, then bring 426 Well Cursed Bones from a successful ritual back to Orgrul.\n426 Well Cursed Bone\nMagram Clan Centaur","desc":"We already know these crystals are capable of more than sundering the ground--the Gelkis have proven that they can be twisted for necromantic power. Do you remember the bones I had you collect? I assembled them as best I could just up the hill. There was enough for two workable skeletons.\n<Orgrul hands you a newly made staff.>\nI will deliver the Necrokhan's staff while you play with your new toy. Return only once you can prove that you know how to use it.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBlade of the Magram Clan Staff of Revelations Desperate Barrier\nExperience: 2,450\n+500 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\n0 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur\nLevel 41 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 37 39 44 52 Side Both factions Quest ID 92873\nThe chain\n15 quests from level 32 to 43, 36,630 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Brutal Politics\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Assault on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram.\nWarug Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Magram Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 33 ] Broken Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Broken Tears to Warug in the Magram Village.\nWarug Desolace\n2,650 XP\n4 [ 40 ] A Conqueror's Crown\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and return a Conqueror's Crown from the Badlands to Warug in Magram Village.\n3,150 XP\n5 [ 40 ] Valley of Bones\nImprove your reputation with the Magram, and locate Orgrul near the Valley of Bones south of Magram Village.\n320 XP\n6 [ 42 ] Mountain of Bones\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 426 Gently Cursed Bones to Orgrul south of the Magram Village in Desolace.\n3,450 XP\n7 [ 42 ] Corrupting Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Petrified Bark and 3 Imbued Tears back to Orgrul.\n3,450 XP\n8 [ 41 ] Proof of Concept this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, then bring 426 Well Cursed Bones from a successful ritual back to Orgrul.\n2,450 XP\n9 [ 40 ] Bone Raising\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and use the Enhanced Necromancy Staff to fully raise undead that are struggling to emerge throughout the Valley of Bones.\n2,350 XP\n[ 42 ] No Mercy for the Weak\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and slay 5 Gelkis Captives scattered around the Valley of Bones.\n2,550 XP\n10 [ 43 ] Bristleback Retreat\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and slay quilboar at Bristleback Retreat.\n3,600 XP\n11 [ 43 ] Long-Term Solutions\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram clan and slay 2 Outcast Scouts, 6 Outcas","cats":["shendralas"]},"6393":{"id":6393,"t":"Elemental War","lv":25,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Incendrites to Tsunaman at Sun Rock Retreat.\n10 Incendrites Rogue Flame Spirit 80 % , Burning Destroyer 80 % , Burning Ravager 80 %","desc":"The Tribunal of the Tides has sent me to wage war on the fire elementals here in Stonetalon Mountain. Neptulon the Tidehunter, Lord of all water elementals, has taken a personal interest in seeing our fiery cousins extinguished.\n‹name›, you can help me gain favor with the Tribunal by destroying the fire elementals in Charred Vale. When destroyed, the fire elementals leave Incendrites. Return these to me and be rewarded.","rew":"Money: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,000","back":"The Tribunal of the Tides grows impatient. They seek to end this war that has raged across all dimensions for eons. My brethren are anxious to hear news of the glorious victory over the hated fire elementals. Have you the Incendrites that I require?","done":"The water spirits within me bubble with the excitement. ‹name›, you have given me a glorious victory to report to the Tribunal of the Tides.\nFor your efforts, I reward you with a choice of my prized possessions.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":47.4,"y":64.2,"n":"Tsunaman","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"393":{"id":393,"t":"Shadow of the Past","lv":29,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Sealed","desc":"of Thredd's Visitor to Master Mathias Shaw in Stormwind.\nSealed Description of Thredd's Visitor\nProvided: Sealed Description of Thredd's Visitor\nDescription\nI really haven't a clue, ‹name›. There is someone else who might be able to help you, and it so happens that he owes me a favor for--well, let's not get into that. Master Mathias Shaw of SI:7 can be found in the barracks in Old Town. Shaw has his thumb on most of the shady, or underhanded dealings of the city.\nIf anyone knows, it'd be him.","rew":"Experience: 600\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Greetings. Of what service can I be to you, ‹class›?","done":"What? What's this? Yes, I think I do know who this man is, but his name is not Maelik. Assassins wear many names and many masks, discarding them as they lose their usefulness. Another alias known to be used by this man is Marzon; though even that is surely not his true name.\nRegardless, he is an assassin and I know a good deal about him.\nMarzon is currently under the employ of Lord Gregor Lescovar, a lord of shady reputation, even given the corruption of the nobility of Stormwind.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":57.7,"y":47.9,"n":"Baros Alexston","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":70.7,"n":"Master Mathias Shaw","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"8553":{"id":8553,"t":"The Captain's Cutlass","lv":50,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 35 instead of 40.","obj":"Speak with Sprogger.","desc":"After I lost my first ship to those giants, I bought another. Named Smotts' Revenge, I filled it with supplies and crew, and set out to find the villains. I found them, but...they beat me. They smashed Smotts' Revenge, killed my second crew and set me on another lifeboat.\nThis time another of the giants, Negolash, stole my cutlass.\nFace Negolash and bring me my cutlass!\nSpeak with Sprogger. He was my cook on the Smotts' Revenge, and survived the last attack. He can help you find the giant.","rew":"Experience: 470","done":"Hello hello, ‹name›. Captain told me you're going after Negolash, eh?","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.7,"y":73.6,"n":"Captain Hecklebury Smotts","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.7,"y":73.6,"n":"Sprogger","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8073":{"id":8073,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Madcap's Tunic","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Bring Falthir the Sightless a Primal Hakkari Aegis. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.\nFalthir the Sightless is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Aegis\nReach 21000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"My eyes failed me long ago, but I do not miss them. Even in a tribe such as ours - where one's vestments convey station and purpose - the most potent of garb exudes power that simple eyes cannot see. The prized tunic of the Zandalar madcap is no exception, exuding the raw power of chaos and madness that they are able to channel.\nThe Paragons of Power I need lie in Zul'Gurub; bring me what I seek, and I will reward you with your own legendary tunic... one befitting a weaver of madness.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Madcap's Tunic\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Welcome back to the Isle, ‹name›... have you returned triumphantly with the Paragons of Power in tow?","done":"Impressive... you have accomplished today what few thought was possible. Your reverence in the tribe is assured for a lifetime, ‹name›. You have earned the right to don the madcap's tunic - do so with our blessing.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.1,"y":13.7,"n":"Falthir the Sightless","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"2873":{"id":2873,"t":"Stoley's Shipment","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Stoley's Shipment to Stoley in Steamwheedle Port.\nStoley's Shipment Stolen Cargo","desc":"I owe \"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley in Booty Bay some rum, to settle a bet, but I'm all out of rum! Captain Cuergo stole my last shipment, and he has it stowed in that walled pirate town to the south.\nIf you can find my shipment of rum and return it to me, then I can prove to MacKinley that Kalimdor's booze beats the dirt out of Booty Bay!","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900","back":"Did you find my shipment of rum, ‹name›?","done":"Great, thanks for the shipment! Now MacKinley and I can finally settle our wager.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":67.1,"y":24,"n":"Stoley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"3513":{"id":3513,"t":"The Runed Scroll","lv":25,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Runed Scroll to the northern guard tower in the Barrens.\nRuned Scroll Aean Swiftriver\nProvided: Runed Scroll","desc":"The official-looking scroll is wrapped tightly with a silvery ribbon. You're sure someone would be interested in seeing this, but who?\nThere is an outpost close to the Ashenvale border to the north, and if the information on this scroll involves the night elves, this would be the place to take it.","rew":"Experience: 2,550\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Whaddya got?","done":"Well now... Where did you find this?","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":48.1,"y":5.4,"n":"Kadrak","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"873":{"id":873,"t":"Isha Awak","lv":27,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Heart of Isha Awak to Mahren Skyseer.\nHeart of Isha Awak Isha Awak","desc":"The grand Isha Awak is lord of these waters. Great is his strength, and solemn his pride. The humans on the coast fear him, for he has consumed many of their number.\nBut I do not fear him. I am grateful he is here. He is a worthy challenge, and honorable prey.\nIf you are ready, then swim out and search for Isha Awak, the Deep Doom.\nHis spirit dwells in his heart, and to hear its beat is to know your fate.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBranding Rod Ward of the Vale\nYou will also receive:\nBeastmaster's Girdle\nExperience: 2,750\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Fear not the waters, ‹race›.","done":"You now are one with Isha Awak, ‹name›. His spirit is with you. He lurks in your eyes...\nEyes that, one day, will learn to see.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":65.8,"y":43.9,"n":"Mahren Skyseer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"96393":{"id":96393,"t":"Old Ironforge Incursion","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Enter the Hall of Thanes beneath Old Ironforge and claim the Head of Durgen Dirgehammer.\nDurgen Dirgehammer's Head","desc":"Gather some allies and head down into the caverns beneath Old Ironforge. Enter the Hall of Thanes there and push to the lower vaults.\nMy Dark Iron is a bit rusty, but I can make out a name--one Durgen Dirgehammer. It's likely that he's the commander. Take his head and deliver it to King Magni Bronzebeard.\nOh, and when you do, tell him his old friend Farsen sends his regards!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCalibrated Blunderbuss Ironforge Greathammer Deepblaze\nMoney: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,200\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"What do ye need, citizen?","done":"A Dark Iron incursion--right beneath our feet? Well, I'm relieved to hear that the Dark Iron commander has been dispatched.\nThe guards will head in and clean up the rest of the rabble. We'll see to it that the breaches are sealed and the lower levels reinforced to ensure that no further incursions are possible.\nThank ye for yer service to Ironforge,‹class›. Take this as a small token of my gratitude. Oh, and if ye see that old Wildhammer rockhugger Farsen again, tell 'em to pay me a proper visit.\nDun Morogh Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":64.8,"y":58.4,"n":"Earthseer Farsen","s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":39.4,"y":55.8,"n":"King Magni Bronzebeard","e":1}],"cats":["the-hall-of-thanes"]},"3913":{"id":3913,"t":"A Grave Situation","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Resurrect, then look for the gravestone that Gaeriyan told you to find.\nLinken's Tempered Sword\nProvided: Linken's Tempered Sword","desc":"If you return to the graveyard, ‹name›, you will find a gravestone there... Not just any gravestone; this one will stand out from the others. Secrets lie within it.\nPush on the stone, and you will learn of these secrets...","rew":"Experience: 2,550","back":"This must be the gravestone that Gaeriyan mentioned...","done":"You push on the stone firmly, and it slides away, revealing a small depression underneath it.\nPlacing Linken's Sword into the depression, you realize that it fits perfectly...","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":53.9,"y":23.3,"n":"Gaeriyan","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":53.8,"y":29.1,"n":"A Conspicuous Gravestone","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"65593":{"id":65593,"t":"Hearts of the lovers","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the hearts of Avelina Lilly and Isaac Pearson to Carendin Halgar in the Temple of the Damned.\nAvelina's Heart\nIsaac's Heart","desc":"An incubus will be drawn to the hearts of lovers, and the most aching love will create the most irresistible lure.\nMy scrying has revealed two that should serve exceptionally.\nIn Silverpine Forest, Avelina Lilly provides her tailoring services to the fallen wizards at Ambermill. In the Barrens, Isaac Pearson hopes to make his mark in the seaside town of Ratchet.\nThey toil on opposite ends of the world, yet their hearts yearn only for each other. Bring those hearts to Carendin.","back":"Ah, ‹name›, you return. Were you able to procure the lovers' hearts?","done":"As expected. Excellently done, ‹name›.\nIdiots.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":85,"y":14.8,"n":"Godrick Farsan","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":85,"y":25.6,"n":"Carendin Halgar","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1513":{"id":1513,"t":"The Binding","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Using Dogran's Pendant, summon and subdue a succubus, then return Dogran's Pendant to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.\nSummoned Succubus slain\nProvided: Dogran's Pendant","desc":"Take this to the summoning circle in Neeru's tent, ‹name›. Summon forth a foul succubus, then show it your mastery. I believe in the strength of your magic. As always, though, be wary, for pride and overconfidence has overcome many a promising warlock.\nWhen you have defeated it, return the pendant to me so that I might deliver the news to Zankaja.","rew":"You will receive:\nSmall Soul Pouch\nYou will learn: Summon Succubus\nExperience: 1,150","back":"When I look upon a succubus, my heart begins to soar... But at the same time, I can almost sense my soul's ebb, drifting away like the tides.\nBe wary, my friend.","done":"Success! Be sure I expected nothing less from my star pupil.\nYou have proven your worth, and gladly will I show you the method of summoning your subdued succubus. Go now, you have much to learn, and when next I see you, I will expect you to have found true mastery over your succubus.\nLeave the sorrow of Dogran and Zankaja to those of us who are longer in years, but remember it, and hold it as protection against the wiles of the dark power you have learned to summon today.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.2,"y":45.3,"n":"Gan'rul Bloodeye","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"153":{"id":153,"t":"Red Leather Bandanas","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 15 Red Leather Bandanas to Scout Galiaan at Sentinel Hill.\n15 Red Leather Bandana Defias Raider 80 % , Defias Looter 80 % , Defias Pillager 80 % , Defias Trapper 80 % and 4 more","desc":"The Defias Front is constantly shifting. I've been following their movements for quite some time now. On a side note, I've ascertained that many members of the gang can be tracked by the Red Leather Bandanas they wear.\nBring me 15 of these Bandanas and I'll see to it you are rewarded.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCloak of the People's Militia Greaves of the People's Militia Leggings of the People's Militia\nExperience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Bring me 15 red leather bandanas and I'll pay you well.","done":"Nice work, ‹race›. Please accept one of these items as payment for all your hard work.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":54,"y":53,"n":"Scout Galiaan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"473":{"id":473,"t":"Report to Captain Stoutfist","lv":28,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Captain Stoutfist.","desc":"‹name›. The Dragonmaw orc clan is showing its strength in more than just Algaz. Captain Stoutfist has asked to speak with those willing to offer aid against these orcs. He is inside the keep, in the war room.","rew":"Experience: 230\n+25 reputation with Ironforge","done":"‹name›. Valstag briefed me on your past success with the Dragonmaw Orcs at Dun Algaz. You're a ‹race› of worth.\nAnd I have a task for you.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.1,"y":56.9,"n":"Valstag Ironjaw","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":9.9,"y":57.5,"n":"Captain Stoutfist","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"633":{"id":633,"t":"The Thandol Span","lv":31,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Destroy the cache of explosives.\nCache of Explosives Destroyed","desc":"Heavens no! Poor Rustlocke. 'Tis quite a tragedy indeed.\nWe must not let his death pass in vain. This parchment you discovered indicates that Kam Deepfury, the mastermind behind the original attack, arranged for a cache of explosives to be stashed just across the Thandol Span, in Arathi Highlands.\nIf those explosives make it to the bridge, our major supply line to the north will be severed! The cache must be destroyed, ‹name›! Return to me when your mission is complete.\nYou're our only hope.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDwarven Guard Cloak Swampland Trousers\nExperience: 2,500\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"The cache of explosives must be destroyed!","done":"The remaining bridge is saved! You have done a great service to King Magni and the people of Khaz Modan.\nNow if we can only hold out long enough for reinforcements to show...\nWetlands Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.9,"y":18.2,"n":"Rhag Garmason","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92473":{"id":92473,"t":"Aggressive encroachment","lv":4,"min":3,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 6 Scrawny Ursera Claws from Scrawny Ursera in Thendal Grove.\n6 Scrawny Ursera Claw","desc":"The ursera den to the southwest is rapidly becoming a problem. Just last week the rangers had to kill an adolescent ursera who wandered too close to the village and attempted to attack a boy playing near the base of the elder tree in the center of the village.\nWe were fortunate that the boy escaped with his life. Hunger and desperation makes these beasts too dangerous to be left unchecked. Go south and put the scrawniest among the ursera down. Bring me their claws as proof when it is done.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nThendal Ranger's Shoes Thendal Ranger's Gloves Thendal Ranger's Belt\nExperience: 360\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"The ursera have grown far more aggressive of late. I wonder what has changed to cause this shift in behavior?","done":"Well done, ‹class›. The Rangers of the Grove are in your debt.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42.4,"y":25,"n":"Valreaa Valewind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92553":{"id":92553,"t":"Restocking the larders","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 3 Small Eggs and 8 Strider Meat from creatures found throughout the Shen'dar Highlands.\n3 Small Egg\n8 Strider Meat","desc":"Up for a bit of work? I could use a bit of muscle from a strong adventuring-type such as yourself. With how dangerous things are getting around here, no one's had much time to hunt or forage of late, and I need someone to get out there and source me fresh eggs and strider meat to keep this village fed.\nI'd be happy to teach you one of my famous recipes if you can bring me what I need. What do you say?","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Skywall Souffle 5 Skywall Souffle\nMoney: 65 0 gold, 0 silver, 65 copper Experience: 410\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"No matter how much things change here on Zephras and how uncertain things get, I always say that a pipe full of dried peacebloom and nice full belly is a comfort that can't be beat!","done":"These eggs aren't easy to get but wind save me, they are DELICIOUS fried up in a bit of ursera tallow.\nIf you've got a bit of time to spare and you enjoy cooking, I can teach you a few tips and tricks I've picked up. Say the word and I'd be happy to train you.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.8,"y":43.8,"n":"Zerril Softbreeze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});